{"id": "pvh-2026-09-05-008", "date": "2026-09-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["pvh"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "PVH beats profit estimates despite 3% sales decline in Q2", "content": "PVH Corp's Q2 2026 revenue fell roughly 3 per cent to $2.1 billion, while adjusted EPS of $3.70 beat analysts' $3.08 estimate by 20 per cent.\nA GAAP net loss of $102.9 million sat behind the beat, with about $107 million in tariff refunds adding roughly $1.80 per share.\nEMEA revenue fell 6 per cent, Calvin Klein dropped 7 per cent and Q3 EPS guidance of $2.50 to $2.65 trailed analysts' $3.17.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pvh-beats-profit-estimates-despite-3-sales-decline-in-q2-313244-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-05-009", "date": "2026-09-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "EU FTA offers India relief, just not fast enough", "content": "Indian textile exporters had one of their toughest years as US tariffs disrupted shipments to the country.\nUS-bound shipments faced combined 50 per cent reciprocal tariffs from August 27, 2025 to February 6, 2026, before duties were reversed.\nICRA projected a 6 to 9 per cent FY2026 revenue decline; TexPro showed Q1 2026 apparel exports to the US down nearly 26 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eu-fta-offers-india-relief-just-not-fast-enough-313239-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-05-010", "date": "2026-09-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "RMG exports from B’desh in green zone as shipment jumps in August 2026", "content": "Bangladesh's RMG exports rose 5.12 per cent to $7.495 billion in July-August 2026, backed by a strong August, EPB provisional data show. \nKnitwear grew 6.17 per cent to $4.193 billion, while woven apparel increased 3.81 per cent to $3.301 billion. \nHome textile exports gained 11.17 per cent to $154.55 million, but cotton and cotton products fell 13.02 per cent to $82.24 million. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/rmg-exports-from-b-desh-in-green-zone-as-shipment-jumps-in-august-2026-313191-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-05-011", "date": "2026-09-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "A meeting that highlights the fraying edges of Bangladesh’s RMG story", "content": "BGMEA told the President that nearly 400 garment factories have closed in Bangladesh over three years, as production costs rose almost 40 per cent. \nInadequate gas supplies, higher energy tariffs, wages and bank interest rates are forcing many factories to operate below half capacity. \nGarment exports contracted 1.64 per cent in FY2025-26 and fell 1.92 per cent in July of FY2026-27. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/a-meeting-that-highlights-the-fraying-edges-of-bangladesh-s-rmg-story-313255-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
